# FIX (spec item 9.1 - "reputation link is broken"): root cause was
# here, not in the app. This is a single-page app - every real "page"
# is a client-side React Router route, not a physical file on the
# static host. Without a catch-all fallback, a cold/fresh request for
# a deep link the host doesn't recognize as a file (e.g.
# /reputation/<token>, opened fresh by a landlord who never loaded the
# app first) fell through to the host's default behavior, which lands
# on /login instead of ever reaching index.html/React Router. Adding
# this wildcard rule - matched only after every specific rule above -
# makes the host serve index.html (200, not a redirect) for any path
# it doesn't otherwise recognize, so React Router's own /reputation/:token
# route (see App.jsx) actually gets a chance to run. This is also what
# was silently making /verify/:paymentId (the receipt QR code
# destination, item 2.1) and /onboard/:token fragile on a cold load -
# same underlying cause, now fixed for all of them at once.
/*  /index.html  200
